@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ktv-nouns`
IMPORT `ktv-annex1-definitions`
IMPORT `ktv-annex5-cancer`
IMPORT `ktv-annex6-early-ci`
IMPORT `ktv-annex7-severe-ci`
IMPORT `ktv-part1-benefits`
IMPORT `ktv-part3-exclusions-and-termination`

-- AIA Khoe Tron Ven V012022 — assessing a claim. No provision of its own: this module puts the
-- layers together in the order a claims assessor reads them, and each arm names the provision
-- that decides it. (1) Is the contract in force on the date of the event? (2) Does the
-- contract still provide this benefit (Article 24)? (3) Is the event the event the benefit
-- needs (the Annex definition, the Article's own conditions)? (4) Has this benefit already been
-- paid (Articles 1(b), 2(b), 3(b)(ii))? (5) Is it excluded (Article 23)? (6) How much (the
-- Article's formula)? Whether the claim was made in time is Article 25, in ktv-part4-claims.l4.

§ `Assessing a claim`

§§ `Cancer — Article 1, Annex 5, Articles 23(c) and 24`

@export Assess a claim for the cancer benefit of an AIA Khoe Tron Ven policy: is it payable, and how much (VND)
GIVEN `the diagnosis` IS A `Diagnosis of cancer` @desc the date of diagnosis and the histopathology findings
      `the context`   IS A `Claim context`       @desc the policy, the account values at the diagnosis, the benefits already paid, whether the contract was in force, and the circumstances
GIVETH AN `Answer to a claim`
`the cancer benefit on` `the diagnosis` `in` `the context` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Annex 5 — the cancer the findings establish` (`the diagnosis`'s `the cancer findings`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `not payable, because` "Annex 5: the findings meet none of the cancer definitions"
    WHEN JUST `the kind`
        THEN BRANCH IF NOT `the context`'s `in force on the date of the event`
                    THEN `not payable, because` "the contract was not in force on the date of diagnosis"
                    IF NOT `Article 24 — the contract still provides` (`the cancer benefit for` `the kind`) `, on` (`the context`'s `the account at the event`) `, after` (`the context`'s `benefits already paid`)
                    THEN `not payable, because` "Article 24: the contract no longer provides this benefit"
                    IF NOT `Article 1(b) — the cancer benefit for` `the kind` `has not yet been paid in` (`the context`'s `benefits already paid`)
                    THEN `not payable, because` "Article 1(b): this cancer benefit has already been paid once"
                    IF `Article 23(c) — under` (`the context`'s `the policy`) `, a cancer or critical-illness benefit for a diagnosis on` (`the diagnosis`'s `date of diagnosis`) `is excluded, given` (`the context`'s `the circumstances`)
                    THEN `not payable, because` "Article 23(c): excluded"
                    OTHERWISE `payable` (`Article 1(a) — the cancer benefit for` `the kind` `, on` (`the context`'s `the account at the event`) `after` (`the context`'s `benefits already paid`))

-- Extended major cancer: Annex 5(4) instead of (1)-(3). Article 23(c) is applied to its date
-- too: it is a cancer benefit.
@export Assess a claim for the extended major cancer benefit of an AIA Khoe Tron Ven policy
GIVEN `the findings` IS A `Findings on extended major cancer` @desc the further finding after the major cancer, and its dates
      `the context`  IS A `Claim context`                     @desc the policy, the account values, the benefits already paid, whether in force, and the circumstances
GIVETH AN `Answer to a claim`
`the extended major cancer benefit on` `the findings` `in` `the context` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the context`'s `in force on the date of the event`
           THEN `not payable, because` "the contract was not in force on the date of the further diagnosis"
           IF NOT `Article 24 — the contract still provides` (`the cancer benefit for` `extended major cancer`) `, on` (`the context`'s `the account at the event`) `, after` (`the context`'s `benefits already paid`)
           THEN `not payable, because` "Article 24: the contract no longer provides this benefit"
           IF NOT `Annex 5(4) — under` (`the context`'s `the policy`) `, extended major cancer is payable on` `the findings`
           THEN `not payable, because` "Annex 5(4): the conditions of extended major cancer are not met"
           IF `Article 23(c) — under` (`the context`'s `the policy`) `, a cancer or critical-illness benefit for a diagnosis on` (`the findings`'s `date of the further diagnosis or confirmation`) `is excluded, given` (`the context`'s `the circumstances`)
           THEN `not payable, because` "Article 23(c): excluded"
           OTHERWISE `payable` (`Article 1(a) — the cancer benefit for` `extended major cancer` `, on` (`the context`'s `the account at the event`) `after` (`the context`'s `benefits already paid`))

§§ `Critical illness — Article 2, Annexes 6 and 7, Articles 23(c) and 24`

@export Assess a claim for an early-stage critical illness benefit of an AIA Khoe Tron Ven policy
GIVEN `the diagnosis` IS A `Diagnosis of an early-stage critical illness`   @desc the date of diagnosis, the general conditions, and the findings on one Annex 6 item
      `the context`   IS A `Claim context`                                  @desc the policy, the account values at the diagnosis, the benefits already paid, whether in force, and the circumstances
GIVETH AN `Answer to a claim`
`the early-stage critical illness benefit on` `the diagnosis` `in` `the context` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the context`'s `in force on the date of the event`
           THEN `not payable, because` "the contract was not in force on the date of diagnosis"
           IF NOT `Article 24 — the contract still provides` (`the early-stage critical illness benefit for` `the condition`) `, on` (`the context`'s `the account at the event`) `, after` (`the context`'s `benefits already paid`)
           THEN `not payable, because` "Article 24: the contract no longer provides this benefit"
           IF NOT `Annex 6 — the diagnosis meets the definition` `the diagnosis`
           THEN `not payable, because` "Annex 6 and Annex 1: the definition is not met"
           IF NOT `Article 2(b) — the early-stage condition` `the condition` `has not yet been paid in` (`the context`'s `benefits already paid`)
           THEN `not payable, because` "Article 2(b): this illness has already been paid once"
           IF `Article 23(c) — under` (`the context`'s `the policy`) `, a cancer or critical-illness benefit for a diagnosis on` (`the diagnosis`'s `date of diagnosis`) `is excluded, given` (`the context`'s `the circumstances`)
           THEN `not payable, because` "Article 23(c): excluded"
           OTHERWISE `payable` (`Article 2(a)(i) — the early-stage critical illness benefit on` (`the context`'s `the account at the event`))
    WHERE
        `the condition` MEANS `Annex 6 — the item the findings are about` (`the diagnosis`'s `the early-stage findings`)

@export Assess a claim for a severe-stage critical illness benefit of an AIA Khoe Tron Ven policy
GIVEN `the diagnosis` IS A `Diagnosis of a severe-stage critical illness`  @desc the date of diagnosis, the general conditions, and the findings on one Annex 7 item
      `the context`   IS A `Claim context`                                 @desc the policy, the account values at the diagnosis, the benefits already paid, whether in force, and the circumstances
GIVETH AN `Answer to a claim`
`the severe-stage critical illness benefit on` `the diagnosis` `in` `the context` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the context`'s `in force on the date of the event`
           THEN `not payable, because` "the contract was not in force on the date of diagnosis"
           IF NOT `Article 24 — the contract still provides` (`the severe-stage critical illness benefit for` `the condition`) `, on` (`the context`'s `the account at the event`) `, after` (`the context`'s `benefits already paid`)
           THEN `not payable, because` "Article 24: the contract no longer provides this benefit"
           IF NOT `Annex 7 — under` (`the context`'s `the policy`) `, the diagnosis meets the definition:` `the diagnosis`
           THEN `not payable, because` "Annex 7 and Annex 1: the definition is not met"
           IF NOT `Article 2(b) — the severe-stage condition` `the condition` `has not yet been paid in` (`the context`'s `benefits already paid`)
           THEN `not payable, because` "Article 2(b): this illness has already been paid once"
           IF `Article 23(c) — under` (`the context`'s `the policy`) `, a cancer or critical-illness benefit for a diagnosis on` (`the diagnosis`'s `date of diagnosis`) `is excluded, given` (`the context`'s `the circumstances`)
           THEN `not payable, because` "Article 23(c): excluded"
           OTHERWISE `payable` (`Article 2(a)(ii) — the severe-stage critical illness benefit on` (`the context`'s `the account at the event`) `after` (`the context`'s `benefits already paid`))
    WHERE
        `the condition` MEANS `Annex 7 — the item the findings are about` (`the diagnosis`'s `the severe-stage findings`)

§§ `Intensive care — Article 3 and Article 24`

-- Article 23 has no exclusion list for the ICU benefit (finding X8).
@export Assess a claim for the intensive care (ICU) benefit of an AIA Khoe Tron Ven policy
GIVEN `the stay`    IS AN `ICU stay`     @desc the stay in the intensive care unit
      `the context` IS A `Claim context` @desc the policy, the account values at the start of treatment, the benefits already paid, whether in force
GIVETH AN `Answer to a claim`
`the ICU benefit on` `the stay` `in` `the context` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the context`'s `in force on the date of the event`
           THEN `not payable, because` "the contract was not in force when ICU treatment began"
           IF NOT `Article 24 — the contract still provides` `the ICU benefit` `, on` (`the context`'s `the account at the event`) `, after` (`the context`'s `benefits already paid`)
           THEN `not payable, because` "Article 24: the contract no longer provides this benefit"
           IF NOT `Article 3(a) — the stay qualifies` `the stay`
           THEN `not payable, because` "Article 3(a): the stay does not qualify"
           IF NOT `Article 3(b) — under` (`the context`'s `the policy`) `, the principles allow the ICU benefit for` `the stay` `after` (`the context`'s `benefits already paid`)
           THEN `not payable, because` "Article 3(b): the age limit or the once-only rule bars it"
           OTHERWISE `payable` (`Article 3(a) — the ICU benefit on` (`the context`'s `the account at the event`) `for` `the stay`)

§§ `Total and permanent disability, and death — Article 6, Annex 1, Articles 23(a), (b) and 24`

@export Assess a claim for the total and permanent disability (TPD) benefit of an AIA Khoe Tron Ven policy
GIVEN `the disablement` IS A Disablement     @desc the losses or the assessed rate, with their dates
      `the context`     IS A `Claim context` @desc the policy, the account values at the disablement, the benefits already paid, whether in force, and the circumstances
GIVETH AN `Answer to a claim`
`the TPD benefit on` `the disablement` `in` `the context` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the context`'s `in force on the date of the event`
           THEN `not payable, because` "the contract was not in force on the date of the insured event"
           IF NOT `Article 24 — the contract still provides` `the TPD benefit` `, on` (`the context`'s `the account at the event`) `, after` (`the context`'s `benefits already paid`)
           THEN `not payable, because` "Article 24: the contract no longer provides this benefit"
           IF NOT `Annex 1 — the insured is totally and permanently disabled` `the disablement`
           THEN `not payable, because` "Annex 1: the insured is not totally and permanently disabled"
           IF NOT `Article 6(a)(i) — under` (`the context`'s `the policy`) `, the age limb holds for` `the disablement`
           THEN `not payable, because` "Article 6(a)(i): the TPD happened after the policy anniversary following age 75"
           IF `Article 23(b) — the TPD benefit is excluded, given` (`the context`'s `the circumstances`)
           THEN `not payable, because` "Article 23(b): excluded"
           OTHERWISE `payable` (`Article 6(a) — the TPD or death benefit on` (`the context`'s `the account at the event`) `after` (`the context`'s `benefits already paid`))

-- Article 23(a) decides the shape of the payment; Article 6 its size.
@export Assess a claim for the death benefit of an AIA Khoe Tron Ven policy
GIVEN `the date of death` IS A DATE                    @desc the date the insured died (ISO 8601)
      `the beneficiaries` IS A LIST OF Beneficiary     @desc each beneficiary's designated share and whether they took part in any fraud
      `the context`       IS A `Claim context`         @desc the policy, the account values at death, the benefits already paid, whether in force, and the circumstances
GIVETH AN `Answer to a claim`
`the death benefit on` `the date of death` `with beneficiaries` `the beneficiaries` `in` `the context` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `the context`'s `in force on the date of the event`
           THEN `not payable, because` "the contract was not in force on the date of death"
           IF NOT `Article 24 — the contract still provides` `the death benefit` `, on` (`the context`'s `the account at the event`) `, after` (`the context`'s `benefits already paid`)
           THEN `not payable, because` "Article 24: the contract no longer provides this benefit"
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER `Article 23(a) — under` (`the context`'s `the policy`) `, the outcome of a death on` `the date of death` `, given` (`the context`'s `the circumstances`)
               WHEN `the death benefit is paid`
                   THEN `payable` `the full benefit`
               WHEN `only the beneficiaries who took no part in the fraud are paid, in their designated shares`
                   THEN `payable` (`Article 23(a)(ii) — the part of` `the full benefit` `paid to the beneficiaries among` `the beneficiaries` `who took no part`)
               WHEN `the contract ends and the contract account value at death is paid`
                   THEN `payable` (`Annex 1 — the contract account value of` (`the context`'s `the account at the event`))
    WHERE
        `the full benefit` MEANS `Article 6(a) — the TPD or death benefit on` (`the context`'s `the account at the event`) `after` (`the context`'s `benefits already paid`)
